5. PURE FIREBASE DATABASE DESIGN (FIRESTORE COLLECTIONS)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
1. users: { uid, email, fullName, role, department, mobile, enrollmentNo, isApproved, isActive }
2. events: { id, title, description, category, department, date, time, venue, status, organizerId, maxParticipants, registeredCount, bannerUrl, averageRating, isTopRated, certificateFee }
3. registrations: { id, eventId, studentId, studentName, enrollmentNo, department, registeredOn, status, qrPassCode }
4. attendance: { id, eventId, studentId, studentName, enrollmentNo, attended, markedOn, checkInMethod, verifiedBy }
5. feedback: { id, eventId, studentId, studentName, organizationRating, relevanceRating, coordinationRating, overallRating, averageScore, comments, isFlagged }
6. certificates: { id, certificateNumber, eventId, eventTitle, studentId, studentName, enrollmentNo, certificateType, feeAmount, isFeePaid, transactionId, verificationQrData }
7. media_gallery: { id, eventId, eventTitle, mediaType, mediaUrl, caption, category, department, uploadedBy, isApproved, isFeatured, likesCount }
8. notifications: { id, recipientId, recipientRole, title, message, eventId, type, isRead, createdAt }
9. contact_queries: { id, name, email, subject, category, message, isResolved, adminReply, submittedOn }


6. PROJECT INSTALLATION & EXECUTION INSTRUCTIONS
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Prerequisites:
- Flutter SDK (Version 3.2.0 or higher) with Dart SDK
- Google Chrome (for Web testing) OR Android Studio / Emulator (for Android APK)

Step-by-step Setup:
1. Open the project root directory in terminal.
2. Run package dependency resolution:
   $ flutter pub get

3. Run the application in Google Chrome:
   $ flutter run -d chrome

4. Run the application on Android Emulator/Device:
   $ flutter run -d android

5. Build Release Android APK:
   $ flutter build apk --release
   (The generated APK will be at build/app/outputs/flutter-apk/app-release.apk)

6. Run Unit and Widget Test Suite:
   $ flutter test


7. LIST OF ASSUMPTIONS & DESIGN DECISIONS
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
1. Color Palette: In strict compliance with user instructions, no purple, violet,
   or magenta colors were used anywhere in the application or assets. The UI uses
   a high-tech collegiate palette of Sapphire Blue, Neon Cyan, Emerald Green, and
   Amber Gold.
2. Certificate Fee Gateway: In accordance with SRS Section 1.4 & 1.6 #6, a simulated
   instant payment gateway (Credit/Debit Card, UPI / QR, and Campus Student Wallet)
   is integrated to process the certificate fee prior to unlocking PDF download.
3. Live Firestore Stream Architecture: All screens bind reactively to Firestore
   streams, ensuring that when an organizer checks in a student or an admin
   approves an event, changes reflect immediately on all devices without reload.
4. Offline Resilience: Built-in local persistence ensures the app functions
   smoothly even when network connectivity on campus is intermittent.


8. VIDEO DEMONSTRATION RECORDING GUIDE (MANDATORY .MP4 SUBMISSION)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
For the competition submission video (.mp4):
1. Introduction (0:00 - 0:30): Show App Logo, Title, and Sitemap on Home Screen.
2. Visitor Flow (0:30 - 1:15): Browse events, search with auto-suggest, view
   campus map, and demonstrate the "Upgrade to Participant" credential modal.
3. Participant Flow (1:15 - 2:30): 1-click register for TechNova Hackathon, open
   My Passes to show digital QR pass, simulate fee payment in Certificate Vault,
   download vector PDF certificate, and submit 4-parameter feedback rating.
4. Organizer Flow (2:30 - 3:45): Open Organizer Control Suite, create a new
   event proposal, demonstrate the interactive QR camera attendance check-in,
   designate competition winners, and broadcast a push announcement.
5. Admin Flow (3:45 - 5:00): Open Admin Dashboard, approve pending event proposals,
   manage user roles, moderate flagged reviews, and export on-demand PDF and
   Excel (.xlsx) analytics reports.
